;
TYPE - DISPLAY AN ORDINARY TEXT FILE

CALLER. Subject to current caller access policy.

A - Display an ordinary text file

:A
DISPLAY AN ORDINARY TEXT FILE

    TYPE DU:filename

Displays an ordinary text file on the terminal.

    TYPE A0:WELCOME.TXT
    TYPE A0:WELCOME.TXT [NO PAGE]

The second example requests output without page pauses. For supported
compressed text or text inside an LBR, use LT instead.

Do not display binary files with TYPE. Control characters in binary
data can confuse your terminal. If you want to keep a file on your own
computer, use the download command rather than screen capture.

See HELP LT, HELP READING and HELP YSEND.

Resident TYPE is a separate wheel-protected RCP implementation. The public
A0:TYPE.COM program documented above is the caller text viewer. To select
the public program explicitly at the console, use A0:TYPE filespec.
